Caelestia shell: Qt 6.8 compatibility patch
============================================

Applies to: caelestia shell pinned at v1.1.1 (e405bf8)
Applied by: install.sh, stage_shell (idempotent, skipped when already applied)

Shell v1.1.1 is the last release that builds against Qt 6.8, but two of
its QML files use things that only exist in Qt 6.9, so the shell fails
to load its configuration on Parrot's Qt 6.8.2:

1. components/effects/Elevation.qml uses RectangularShadow from
   QtQuick.Effects, a type introduced in Qt 6.9. This patch rewrites
   Elevation on top of MultiEffect (available since Qt 6.5), keeping
   the exact public surface every consumer sets: level, dp, radius.
   The shadow is rendered by MultiEffect over a rounded rectangle
   source, with the same colour, blur curve and vertical offset.
2. modules/bar/Bar.qml uses DelegateChooser without an import. The
   type moved to QtQml.Models in Qt 6.9; on Qt 6.8 it still lives in
   Qt.labs.qmlmodels. This patch adds `import Qt.labs.qmlmodels`,
   which also exists on Qt 6.9+, so the file loads on both.

Proven live on Parrot Security 7.4, Qt 6.8.2 (KDE Plasma Wayland
session): with this patch the full shell configuration loads and the
bar renders. Companion fix in install.sh stage_lib: the core library's
unversioned libcaelestia.so symlink must not shadow the QML backing
library of the same name, or the Caelestia QML plugin fails to load
with an undefined qml_register_types_Caelestia symbol.

diff --git a/components/effects/Elevation.qml b/components/effects/Elevation.qml
index fb29f16..d88ddeb 100644
--- a/components/effects/Elevation.qml
+++ b/components/effects/Elevation.qml
@@ -3,14 +3,36 @@ import qs.services
 import QtQuick
 import QtQuick.Effects
 
-RectangularShadow {
+// Qt 6.8 compatibility: upstream uses RectangularShadow from
+// QtQuick.Effects, a type that only exists in Qt 6.9+. This replacement
+// renders the same elevation shadow with MultiEffect (available since
+// Qt 6.5) over a rounded rectangle source. The public surface is
+// unchanged: level, dp and radius, as set by every consumer.
+Item {
+    id: root
+
     property int level
     property real dp: [0, 1, 3, 6, 8, 12][level]
+    property real radius: 0
+
+    Rectangle {
+        id: shadowSource
 
-    color: Qt.alpha(Colours.palette.m3shadow, 0.7)
-    blur: (dp * 5) ** 0.7
-    spread: -dp * 0.3 + (dp * 0.1) ** 2
-    offset.y: dp / 2
+        anchors.fill: parent
+        radius: root.radius
+        color: "black"
+        visible: false
+    }
+
+    MultiEffect {
+        anchors.fill: parent
+        source: shadowSource
+        shadowEnabled: true
+        shadowColor: Qt.alpha(Colours.palette.m3shadow, 0.7)
+        blurMax: 64
+        shadowBlur: Math.min(1, ((root.dp * 5) ** 0.7) / 64)
+        shadowVerticalOffset: root.dp / 2
+    }
 
     Behavior on dp {
         Anim {}
diff --git a/modules/bar/Bar.qml b/modules/bar/Bar.qml
index 0382b5d..ce741f4 100644
--- a/modules/bar/Bar.qml
+++ b/modules/bar/Bar.qml
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@ import "components/workspaces"
 import Quickshell
 import QtQuick
 import QtQuick.Layouts
+import Qt.labs.qmlmodels
 
 ColumnLayout {
     id: root
